<section class="about wrap"><h1>About</h1><p>I am interested in code auditing, vulnerability mechanisms, network forensics and the trust boundaries inside systems. These notes aim to make the reasoning visible: how a question is framed, what an observation establishes, and where the evidence stops.</p><p>Current topics include AI agents, tool invocation, runtime authorization and security evaluation.</p><figure class="identity-art"><img src="/assets/emergence.png" width="192" height="192" alt="An irregular charcoal ring with fine contours, scattered pixels and a copper seam" decoding="async"><figcaption><strong>Emergence</strong><span>Local rules form a larger structure. The open center represents a boundary to understand and protect; the copper seam marks a path of inquiry.</span></figcaption></figure><a class="text-link" href="/writing/">Browse writing →</a></section>
